data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — erc-4626@final\n_human-validated 2026-08-12 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/erc-4626/tokenized-vault.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-12, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test, fork\n- chains exercised: ethereum\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n\n# Recipe: erc-4626 @1 :: tokenized-vault\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-12 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 6 quotes · 9 structural · 7 fork assertions against FOUR LIVE MAINNET VAULTS. chains: [ethereum]. (Banner, footer, RUN.md and stamp changed in ONE edit — C3 now asserts all four, after #13's footer was found still printing another recipe's stamp. Session log 2026-08-12.)\nproject_id: \"erc-4626\"      # the STANDARD's id, as the locked P1 worklist has it\nversion_major: 1            # ⚠ SEE SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §7. An ERC has no major. `1` means \"the\n                            #   standard, which is Final and has exactly one version\". A FOURTH\n                            #   meaning for the axis in this repo, after dynamic, permit2, across.\nversion: \"final\"            # ⚠ NOT a semver and NOT a commit. An ERC's version identity IS its\n                            #   status; the pinned commit is recorded in `provenance` instead.\ntype: \"tokenized-vault\"\n\n# ⚠ ETHEREUM ONLY, and narrow on purpose. The four sampled vaults are mainnet deployments; V5 ran\n# the shipped example against each of them. This recipe makes NO claim about vaults on any other\n# chain — the same restraint #17 applied when its flow ran on one chain of three.\nchains: [ethereum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ These are the CONFORMANCE SAMPLE, not \"the\" ERC-4626 deployments. A standard has no canonical\n# address. Every count in this recipe says \"of four\" for that reason.#\n# ⚠ F-4 CURATOR RULING 2026-08-15 — LEFT AS LABELS ON PURPOSE, NOT AN OVERSIGHT.\n#   These four are VAULT INSTANCES: examples OF the ERC-4626 standard, not deployments of it. A\n#   standard has no deployment, and nesting them under `ethereum` would assert that erc-4626 is\n#   deployed at these addresses — false, and a number improved by relabelling something that was\n#   already right is worse than the red number. All four DO carry code on ethereum (measured\n#   2026-08-15); that is what makes them a usable conformance sample, and it is not what would\n#   make them a deployment of this recipe's own subject.\ndeployments:\n  sDAI: \"0x83F20F44975D03b1b09e64809B757c47f942BEeA\"\n  sUSDS: \"0xa3931d71877C0E7a3148CB7Eb4463524FEc27fbD\"\n  steakUSDC: \"0xBEEF01735c132Ada46AA9aA4c54623cAA92A64CB\"\n  gtUSDC: \"0xdd0f28e19C1780eb6396170735D45153D261490d\"\n\n\n# ── THE CHAIN OF EACH ADDRESS ABOVE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ ADDED 2026-08-20 (amendment A1) SO THE FACT IS MACHINE-READABLE, NOT SO IT IS NEW. The\n# comment above `deployments` already stated it in prose; a typed-table writer cannot read prose,\n# and it correctly REFUSED to write rows rather than infer the chain from `chains:` — inferring\n# is what C50 forbids.\n#\n# 🔴 THIS IS A SIBLING FIELD, AND `deployments:` IS DELIBERATELY LEFT FLAT. Nesting these under\n# `ethereum` is what the F-4 curator ruling of 2026-08-15 REFUSED, for a reason that has not\n# changed: it would assert that THIS RECIPE'S SUBJECT is deployed at these addresses. This field\n# says something narrower and true — which chain each ADDRESS lives on — and asserts nothing about\n# the subject.\n#\n# ⚠ `chains:` IS A DIFFERENT FACT AND IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE. That list is the chains this recipe\n# EXERCISED; this map is where each address is. They coincide here, and a reader deriving one from\n# the other would be right by accident.\n#\n# Every entry below was verified on 2026-08-20 by a read-only `eth_getCode` against the named\n# chain's public RPC — receipts in amendment A1. `is_contract` records what that probe returned.\ndeployment_chains:\n  sDAI: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 10,925 bytes of code, symbol \"sDAI\", decimals 18\n  sUSDS: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 170 bytes of code, symbol \"sUSDS\", decimals 18\n  steakUSDC: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 19,340 bytes of code, symbol \"steakUSDC\", decimals 18\n  gtUSDC: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 19,340 bytes of code, symbol \"gtUSDC\", decimals 18\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ── THE ROUNDING MATRIX ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ PLACED HERE, BEFORE THE EXAMPLE, ON PURPOSE. The serving path is prefix truncation and at the\n#   default budget it reaches ~18% of this body, while `common_mistakes` begins at 29%. The full\n#   entry lives there; this is the part a consumer must not receive half of. ⭐ A CHUNK BOUNDARY\n#   SERVED HALF THIS RULE TO A REAL CONSUMER — both directions are therefore adjacent, in one\n#   field, quoted verbatim from the spec at its pin.\nrounding_matrix:\n  principle: \"Every direction favours the VAULT over the user. Whichever side you are on, expect\n              the worse of the two roundings.\"\n  round_down: \"- If (1) it's calculating how many shares to issue to a user for a certain amount of the underlying tokens they provide or (2) it's determining the amount of the underlying tokens to transfer to them for returning a certain amount of shares, it should round _down_.\"\n  round_up: \"- If (1) it's calculating the amount of shares a user has to supply to receive a given amount of the underlying tokens or (2) it's calculating the amount of underlying tokens a user has to provide to receive a certain amount of shares, it should round _up_.\"\n  in_practice:\n    deposit: \"assets in → shares out · rounds DOWN · you may receive fewer shares than the naive ratio\"\n    redeem: \"shares in → assets out · rounds DOWN · you may receive fewer assets\"\n    mint: \"shares out ← assets charged · rounds UP · BUDGET MORE ASSETS THAN THE NAIVE RATIO\"\n    withdraw: \"assets out ← shares charged · rounds UP · BUDGET MORE SHARES THAN THE NAIVE RATIO\"\n  the_exception: \"`convertToShares` and `convertToAssets` MUST BOTH always round _down_, which is\n              why they are not substitutes for the preview functions — see mistake #3. The spec\n              tells integrators wanting a rounded-up conversion to add 1 wei themselves.\"\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 45319 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:erc-4626@final::tokenized-vault::body@6055\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/blob/cf8bff877b00d56cec0c60007a25bae0937d0d03/ERCS/erc-4626.md\n- https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/ERC4626.sol\n- https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com\n- https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/tree/cf8bff877b00d56cec0c60007a25bae0937d0d03\n\n---\n\n### 3deffd1d-74fb-5f57-b7f7-ddf107cf77b2\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L29-L39\n\n```\nSpecification\nAll [EIP-4626](./eip-4626.md) tokenized Vaults MUST implement EIP-20 to represent shares.\nIf a Vault is to be non-transferrable, it MAY revert on calls to `transfer` or `transferFrom`.\nThe EIP-20 operations `balanceOf`, `transfer`, `totalSupply`, etc. operate on the Vault…\n```\n\n### 4a3ebb69-5a2a-579c-8b1b-8b699139da69\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L1-L12\n\n```\n---\neip: 4626\ntitle: Tokenized Vaults\ndescription: Tokenized Vaults with a single underlying EIP-20 token.\nauthor: Joey Santoro (@joeysantoro), t11s (@transmissions11), Jet Jadeja (@JetJadeja), Alberto Cuesta Cañada (@alcueca), Señor Doggo (@fubuloubu)\ndiscussions-to:…\n```\n\n### fa1e4310-49c8-5861-9af7-eb549bb15041\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L597-L601\n\n```\nSecurity Considerations\nIntegrators of EIP-4626 Vaults should be aware of the difference between these view methods when integrating with this standard. Additionally, note that the amount of underlying assets a user may receive from redeeming their Vault shares (`previewRedeem`) can be…\n```\n\n### bf39a19a-6cc4-593c-9997-e8aad525b761\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L603-L608\n\n```\nSecurity Considerations\n- If (1) it's calculating the amount of shares a user has to supply to receive a given amount of the underlying tokens or (2) it's calculating the amount of underlying tokens a user has to provide to receive a certain amount of shares, it should round _up_.\n\nThe only…\n```\n\n### e255a23d-29c0-50ac-812f-7ced8d6899b7\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L553-L566\n\n```\nRationale\nThe Vault interface is designed to be optimized for integrators with a feature complete yet minimal interface.\nDetails such as accounting and allocation of deposited tokens are intentionally not specified,\nas Vaults are expected to be treated as black boxes on-chain and inspected…\n```\n\n### 6abc28e4-a55f-5b74-8595-0e7642c89db1\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L525-L551\n\n```\nSpecification › Events › Withdraw\n`sender` has exchanged `shares`, owned by `owner`, for `assets`, and transferred those `assets` to `receiver`.\n\nMUST be emitted when shares are withdrawn from the Vault in `EIP-4626.redeem` or `EIP-4626.withdraw` methods.\n\n```yaml\n- name: Withdraw\n  type: event…\n```\n\n### a80224f7-8edd-5a47-bc1c-bbe54f3786cc\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L572-L575\n\n```\nBackwards Compatibility\nEIP-4626 is fully backward compatible with the EIP-20 standard and has no known compatibility issues with other standards.\nFor production implementations of Vaults which do not use EIP-4626, wrapper adapters can be developed and used.\n```\n\n### d109e4a6-f710-5b88-b2d9-f9c423ff3519\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L21-L27\n\n```\nMotivation\nTokenized Vaults have a lack of standardization leading to diverse implementation details.\nSome various examples include lending markets, aggregators, and intrinsically interest bearing tokens.\nThis makes integration difficult at the aggregator or plugin layer for protocols which need…\n```\n\n### 5db690db-2a48-5a47-a9dc-d1ed509c61e2\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L14-L19\n\n```\nAbstract\nThe following standard allows for the implementation of a standard API for tokenized Vaults\nrepresenting shares of a single underlying [EIP-20](./eip-20.md) token.\nThis standard is an extension on the EIP-20 token that provides basic functionality for depositing\nand withdrawing tokens and…\n```\n\n### d362b95a-bad9-5e67-8e7e-31b769d997d5\n`erc-4626@final` · repo:8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d · as_of 2026-08-03T21:38:58Z\nhttps://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L577-L583\n\n```\nReference Implementation\nSee [Solmate EIP-4626](https://github.com/transmissions11/solmate/blob/main/src/tokens/ERC4626.sol):\na minimal and opinionated implementation of the standard with hooks for developers to easily insert custom logic into deposits and withdrawals.\n\nSee [Vyper…\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"erc-4626","version":"final","recipe_type":"tokenized-vault","last_validated":"2026-08-12","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-12","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test","fork"],"chains_exercised":["ethereum"],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.","gas":"see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition."},"body":"# Recipe: erc-4626 @1 :: tokenized-vault\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-12 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 6 quotes · 9 structural · 7 fork assertions against FOUR LIVE MAINNET VAULTS. chains: [ethereum]. (Banner, footer, RUN.md and stamp changed in ONE edit — C3 now asserts all four, after #13's footer was found still printing another recipe's stamp. Session log 2026-08-12.)\nproject_id: \"erc-4626\"      # the STANDARD's id, as the locked P1 worklist has it\nversion_major: 1            # ⚠ SEE SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §7. An ERC has no major. `1` means \"the\n                            #   standard, which is Final and has exactly one version\". A FOURTH\n                            #   meaning for the axis in this repo, after dynamic, permit2, across.\nversion: \"final\"            # ⚠ NOT a semver and NOT a commit. An ERC's version identity IS its\n                            #   status; the pinned commit is recorded in `provenance` instead.\ntype: \"tokenized-vault\"\n\n# ⚠ ETHEREUM ONLY, and narrow on purpose. The four sampled vaults are mainnet deployments; V5 ran\n# the shipped example against each of them. This recipe makes NO claim about vaults on any other\n# chain — the same restraint #17 applied when its flow ran on one chain of three.\nchains: [ethereum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ These are the CONFORMANCE SAMPLE, not \"the\" ERC-4626 deployments. A standard has no canonical\n# address. Every count in this recipe says \"of four\" for that reason.#\n# ⚠ F-4 CURATOR RULING 2026-08-15 — LEFT AS LABELS ON PURPOSE, NOT AN OVERSIGHT.\n#   These four are VAULT INSTANCES: examples OF the ERC-4626 standard, not deployments of it. A\n#   standard has no deployment, and nesting them under `ethereum` would assert that erc-4626 is\n#   deployed at these addresses — false, and a number improved by relabelling something that was\n#   already right is worse than the red number. All four DO carry code on ethereum (measured\n#   2026-08-15); that is what makes them a usable conformance sample, and it is not what would\n#   make them a deployment of this recipe's own subject.\ndeployments:\n  sDAI: \"0x83F20F44975D03b1b09e64809B757c47f942BEeA\"\n  sUSDS: \"0xa3931d71877C0E7a3148CB7Eb4463524FEc27fbD\"\n  steakUSDC: \"0xBEEF01735c132Ada46AA9aA4c54623cAA92A64CB\"\n  gtUSDC: \"0xdd0f28e19C1780eb6396170735D45153D261490d\"\n\n\n# ── THE CHAIN OF EACH ADDRESS ABOVE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ ADDED 2026-08-20 (amendment A1) SO THE FACT IS MACHINE-READABLE, NOT SO IT IS NEW. The\n# comment above `deployments` already stated it in prose; a typed-table writer cannot read prose,\n# and it correctly REFUSED to write rows rather than infer the chain from `chains:` — inferring\n# is what C50 forbids.\n#\n# 🔴 THIS IS A SIBLING FIELD, AND `deployments:` IS DELIBERATELY LEFT FLAT. Nesting these under\n# `ethereum` is what the F-4 curator ruling of 2026-08-15 REFUSED, for a reason that has not\n# changed: it would assert that THIS RECIPE'S SUBJECT is deployed at these addresses. This field\n# says something narrower and true — which chain each ADDRESS lives on — and asserts nothing about\n# the subject.\n#\n# ⚠ `chains:` IS A DIFFERENT FACT AND IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE. That list is the chains this recipe\n# EXERCISED; this map is where each address is. They coincide here, and a reader deriving one from\n# the other would be right by accident.\n#\n# Every entry below was verified on 2026-08-20 by a read-only `eth_getCode` against the named\n# chain's public RPC — receipts in amendment A1. `is_contract` records what that probe returned.\ndeployment_chains:\n  sDAI: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 10,925 bytes of code, symbol \"sDAI\", decimals 18\n  sUSDS: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 170 bytes of code, symbol \"sUSDS\", decimals 18\n  steakUSDC: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 19,340 bytes of code, symbol \"steakUSDC\", decimals 18\n  gtUSDC: { chain: \"ethereum\", is_contract: true }\n  # 19,340 bytes of code, symbol \"gtUSDC\", decimals 18\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ── THE ROUNDING MATRIX ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ PLACED HERE, BEFORE THE EXAMPLE, ON PURPOSE. The serving path is prefix truncation and at the\n#   default budget it reaches ~18% of this body, while `common_mistakes` begins at 29%. The full\n#   entry lives there; this is the part a consumer must not receive half of. ⭐ A CHUNK BOUNDARY\n#   SERVED HALF THIS RULE TO A REAL CONSUMER — both directions are therefore adjacent, in one\n#   field, quoted verbatim from the spec at its pin.\nrounding_matrix:\n  principle: \"Every direction favours the VAULT over the user. Whichever side you are on, expect\n              the worse of the two roundings.\"\n  round_down: \"- If (1) it's calculating how many shares to issue to a user for a certain amount of the underlying tokens they provide or (2) it's determining the amount of the underlying tokens to transfer to them for returning a certain amount of shares, it should round _down_.\"\n  round_up: \"- If (1) it's calculating the amount of shares a user has to supply to receive a given amount of the underlying tokens or (2) it's calculating the amount of underlying tokens a user has to provide to receive a certain amount of shares, it should round _up_.\"\n  in_practice:\n    deposit: \"assets in → shares out · rounds DOWN · you may receive fewer shares than the naive ratio\"\n    redeem: \"shares in → assets out · rounds DOWN · you may receive fewer assets\"\n    mint: \"shares out ← assets charged · rounds UP · BUDGET MORE ASSETS THAN THE NAIVE RATIO\"\n    withdraw: \"assets out ← shares charged · rounds UP · BUDGET MORE SHARES THAN THE NAIVE RATIO\"\n  the_exception: \"`convertToShares` and `convertToAssets` MUST BOTH always round _down_, which is\n              why they are not substitutes for the preview functions — see mistake #3. The spec\n              tells integrators wanting a rounded-up conversion to add 1 wei themselves.\"","source_path":"recipes/erc-4626/tokenized-vault.yaml","requested_version":null,"exact_version_match":null,"body_truncated":true,"body_bytes":45319,"citations":["https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/blob/cf8bff877b00d56cec0c60007a25bae0937d0d03/ERCS/erc-4626.md","https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/ERC4626.sol","https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com","https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/tree/cf8bff877b00d56cec0c60007a25bae0937d0d03"],"citations_capped":false,"body_cursor":"recipe:erc-4626@final::tokenized-vault::body@6055"},"hits":[{"selector":"3deffd1d-74fb-5f57-b7f7-ddf107cf77b2","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L29-L39","snippet":"Specification\nAll [EIP-4626](./eip-4626.md) tokenized Vaults MUST implement EIP-20 to represent shares.\nIf a Vault is to be non-transferrable, it MAY revert on calls to `transfer` or `transferFrom`.\nThe EIP-20 operations `balanceOf`, `transfer`, `totalSupply`, etc. operate on the Vault…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"4a3ebb69-5a2a-579c-8b1b-8b699139da69","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L1-L12","snippet":"---\neip: 4626\ntitle: Tokenized Vaults\ndescription: Tokenized Vaults with a single underlying EIP-20 token.\nauthor: Joey Santoro (@joeysantoro), t11s (@transmissions11), Jet Jadeja (@JetJadeja), Alberto Cuesta Cañada (@alcueca), Señor Doggo (@fubuloubu)\ndiscussions-to:…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"fa1e4310-49c8-5861-9af7-eb549bb15041","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L597-L601","snippet":"Security Considerations\nIntegrators of EIP-4626 Vaults should be aware of the difference between these view methods when integrating with this standard. Additionally, note that the amount of underlying assets a user may receive from redeeming their Vault shares (`previewRedeem`) can be…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"bf39a19a-6cc4-593c-9997-e8aad525b761","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L603-L608","snippet":"Security Considerations\n- If (1) it's calculating the amount of shares a user has to supply to receive a given amount of the underlying tokens or (2) it's calculating the amount of underlying tokens a user has to provide to receive a certain amount of shares, it should round _up_.\n\nThe only…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"e255a23d-29c0-50ac-812f-7ced8d6899b7","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L553-L566","snippet":"Rationale\nThe Vault interface is designed to be optimized for integrators with a feature complete yet minimal interface.\nDetails such as accounting and allocation of deposited tokens are intentionally not specified,\nas Vaults are expected to be treated as black boxes on-chain and inspected…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"6abc28e4-a55f-5b74-8595-0e7642c89db1","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L525-L551","snippet":"Specification › Events › Withdraw\n`sender` has exchanged `shares`, owned by `owner`, for `assets`, and transferred those `assets` to `receiver`.\n\nMUST be emitted when shares are withdrawn from the Vault in `EIP-4626.redeem` or `EIP-4626.withdraw` methods.\n\n```yaml\n- name: Withdraw\n  type: event…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"a80224f7-8edd-5a47-bc1c-bbe54f3786cc","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L572-L575","snippet":"Backwards Compatibility\nEIP-4626 is fully backward compatible with the EIP-20 standard and has no known compatibility issues with other standards.\nFor production implementations of Vaults which do not use EIP-4626, wrapper adapters can be developed and used.","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"d109e4a6-f710-5b88-b2d9-f9c423ff3519","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L21-L27","snippet":"Motivation\nTokenized Vaults have a lack of standardization leading to diverse implementation details.\nSome various examples include lending markets, aggregators, and intrinsically interest bearing tokens.\nThis makes integration difficult at the aggregator or plugin layer for protocols which need…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"5db690db-2a48-5a47-a9dc-d1ed509c61e2","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L14-L19","snippet":"Abstract\nThe following standard allows for the implementation of a standard API for tokenized Vaults\nrepresenting shares of a single underlying [EIP-20](./eip-20.md) token.\nThis standard is an extension on the EIP-20 token that provides basic functionality for depositing\nand withdrawing tokens and…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"},{"selector":"d362b95a-bad9-5e67-8e7e-31b769d997d5","source_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ercs/blob/8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d/ERCS/erc-4626.md#L577-L583","snippet":"Reference Implementation\nSee [Solmate EIP-4626](https://github.com/transmissions11/solmate/blob/main/src/tokens/ERC4626.sol):\na minimal and opinionated implementation of the standard with hooks for developers to easily insert custom logic into deposits and withdrawals.\n\nSee [Vyper…","project":"erc-4626","version":"final","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-14T16:14:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T21:38:58Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"8577735a86e50ffdde19c157158ba015bfbc143d"}],"scope":{"projects":["erc-4626"],"version":null,"version_defaulted":false,"abstained":false,"source":"identifier","version_match":"not-requested","names_project":true,"diagnostics":{"naming_via":["erc4626"]},"explanation":"identifiers scope to erc-4626"},"estimated_tokens":1968,"truncated":false,"top_body":"disabled","content_rescue":true}},"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1}

